{
 "work": "Popol Vuh (Ximénez manuscript, Newberry Ayer MS 1515)",
 "notes": [
  "Cut by page images, three to a part: images 0012 onward, the pilot (popol-vuh-001) having covered 0009–0011 and the first line of 0012. The text runs to image 0124 (the genealogy of the lords ends there; 0125 begins Ximénez's Escolios).",
  "A part's text is established in its own firing: it begins exactly where the previous part's established text ends, and runs to the last sentence that ends on its last image; a sentence that runs over the edge of the last image is finished from the next image. The establishing firing names the part and records the folios.",
  "Images are in source/pages/i<NNNN>.jpg: the left (K'iche') column of each page at 40% of the Library of Congress master, background flattened. A sharper crop of any spot: https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:gdc:gdcwdl:wd:l_:19:99:5:wdl_19995:ayer_ms_1515_vol_2_<NNNN>/<x,y,w,h>/pct:100/0/default.jpg if the sandbox reaches it (send a browser User-Agent).",
  "The Library of Congress has no image 0086 or 0102 (both answer 404; checked 2026-11-20). Judging by Ximénez's page numbers on the neighbouring images, no page of the manuscript seems to be lost there. If the text does not run on across either point, follow README rule 7: leave the smallest gap, note it for the reader, record it in QUESTIONS.md, and carry on."
 ],
